brand: Ride
model name: Psychocandy
model year: 2027
AUD price: $949.99
availability: Preorder
estimated availability date: May 1, 2026
board type: Freeride - Powder
rider level: Intermediate
flex: Medium - Stiff
shape: Tapered Directional (tail narrower than nose for enhanced control and stability in deeper snow)
camber type: Directional Zero Camber (directional shape with flat zone underfoot, extended rocker in nose and tail)
width: Standard
sidecut type: Tapered Bi-Radial Sidecut (underfoot width of a wide board with maintained tip/tail width; enhances leverage on landings, improves grip through turns, provides stability on flat base)
mounting pattern: 2x4 Inserts
available lengths: 146cm, 150cm, 154cm, 158cm
sizing recommendation: Size down 3-6cm from normal size
design inspiration: Inspired by the Warpig
gender: Unisex
topsheet: Topless Topsheet (eliminates need for topsheet by transferring graphics directly to fiberglass; enhances durability, reduces weight, minimises raw material usage)
laminate: Carbon Infused Glass, Carbon Array 5, Double Impact Plates
laminate detail carbon infused glass: 90° carbon fibers woven into glass for added pop and response without increasing stiffness
laminate detail carbon array 5: Power distribution technology with five carbon stringers in binding zone for complete board control at every stance position; rider input directed to opposite contact point
laminate detail double impact plates: Two layer urethane weaves beneath each binding area for compressive strength, preventing board breaks
core: Performance Light Core (blend of high-strength Aspen, Bamboo, and lightweight Paulownia wood for ideal balance of strength and lightness)
sidewall: Carbon Slimewalls, Roll-In Construction (blends layers of carbon and Slimewall material from inserts to contact points for pop, stability, and responsiveness; smooth and damp ride)
sidewall detail roll-in: 3D structure surrounds urethane Slimewall sidewalls to enhance board strength, prevent topsheet chipping, and reduce weight
base: Sintered, Stone Ground Base (premium 4000 PTEX material; heating and compressing polyethylene particles for porous structure; durable, fast)
edges: Standard Steel Edge
tip/tail construction: Thin Con (tapered tips and tails to reduce swing weight, improve tip flex, boost overall durability)
resin: Bio Resin (plant-based epoxy from renewable resources like vegetable oils, reduced carbon footprint)
